{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7334422","formula":"C₂₁H₂₇N₃","hill":"C21H27N3","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":27.0,"N":3.0},"names":{"en":"Rimcazole"},"descriptions":{"en":"Rimcazole is an antagonist of the sigma receptor as well as a dopamine reuptake inhibitor. Sigma receptors are thought to be involved in the drug psychosis that can be induced by some drugs such as phencyclidine and cocaine, and rimcazole was originally researched as a potential antipsychotic with a different mechanism of action to traditional antipsychotic drugs, although common with butyrophenone antipsychotics such as haloperidol. Trials proved inconclusive and rimcazole was not pursued for this application, but other sigma antagonists continue to be researched for a variety of potential applications."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":53389,"mass":321.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@@H]1CN(C[C@@H](N1)C)CCCN2C3=CC=CC=C3C4=CC=CC=C42","inchikey":"GUDVQJXODNJRIJ-CALCHBBNSA-N","iupac":"9-[3-[(3R,5S)-3,5-dimethylpiperazin-1-yl]propyl]carbazole","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"53389","atoms":51,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.525,"y":0.312,"z":-0.117,"el":"N"},{"x":-5.371,"y":0.011,"z":-0.56,"el":"N"},{"x":1.652,"y":0.434,"z":0.944,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.817,"y":1.228,"z":0.049,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.389,"y":-0.613,"z":-1.456,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.504,"y":0.927,"z":0.79,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.076,"y":-0.913,"z":-0.714,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.274,"y":0.03,"z":0.585,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.655,"y":1.324,"z":1.108,"el":"C"},{"x":0.666,"y":1.05,"z":1.825,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.851,"y":1.82,"z":1.005,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.986,"y":-1.896,"z":-2.032,"el":"C"},{"x":2.548,"y":1.135,"z":0.181,"el":"C"},{"x":1.8,"y":-0.917,"z":0.777,"el":"C"},{"x":3.311,"y":0.195,"z":-0.513,"el":"C"},{"x":2.838,"y":-1.102,"z":-0.137,"el":"C"